module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.ChaoticHigherDirectImage

/-!
# What Stacks 07JK really asks of Stacks 07JJ

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` of [Stacks, Tag 07MF] with `X` and `S`
affine, and let `u = wholeToAffineSubsite : 𝒞 ⥤ AffineCris(X/S)` be the inclusion of the chaotic
subsite of thickenings of the whole of `X`.

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/ChaoticHigherDirectImage.lean` reduces step 4
of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JK] — the vanishing `R^p f_* F = 0` for `p > 0` — to the hypothesis
`Vanishing07JJ`, which asks the cohomology of the localized site `Cris(X/S)/(U, T, δ)` to vanish
in positive degrees for **every** object with affine ambient scheme.

That is more than the proof uses.  The reduction evaluates the hypothesis only at the objects
`u V` for `V` an object of `𝒞`, that is, only at divided power thickenings of the *whole* of `X`.
This file records the narrower hypothesis and redoes the reduction from it, so that whoever proves
[Stacks, Tag 07JJ] knows which objects it is actually needed at.

The gap is not closed here and no `07JJ` or `07JK` attribute is placed: `Vanishing07JJWhole` is
still an unproved hypothesis.  What changes is its size.  Two things are worth recording about
what remains.

First, like `Vanishing07JJ`, this hypothesis is stated for an arbitrary abelian sheaf and is false
at that generality: positive-degree vanishing over an affine object is a property of locally
quasi-coherent modules, not of abelian sheaves, and the topology of `Cris(X/S)` is generated by
the restriction covers of
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck`, so an abelian sheaf with
nonvanishing Čech `H^1` on a Zariski cover of an affine ambient scheme is a counterexample.  A
proof has to restrict to a module.

Second, it can be so restricted, in the form `Vanishing07JJWhole S (SmallSite.abelianSheaf F)`
with `F` locally quasi-coherent: `SmallSite.abelianSheaf` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/AffineCohomology.lean` lifts the underlying
abelian sheaf of a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules to the coefficient universe `u + 1` along
`AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor`, which preserves limits of every size.

## Main definitions

Everything below lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `Vanishing07JJWhole` — the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ] asked only at the divided power
  thickenings of the whole of `X`.

## Main results

* `vanishing07JJWhole_of_vanishing07JJ` — the narrower hypothesis follows from the wider one, so
  nothing is lost by using it.
* **`isZero_higherDirectImageToWhole_of_vanishing07JJWhole`** — `R^p f_* F|_{AffineCris} = 0` for
  `p > 0` from the narrower hypothesis: step 4 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JK] needs 07JJ only
  at thickenings of the whole of `X`.

## Implementation notes

The composite `u ⋙ affineι` is the inclusion `wholeι : 𝒞 ⥤ Cris(X/S)` definitionally, which is
what lets the narrower hypothesis be applied where the wider one was: the object at which the
reduction evaluates it is `wholeι V`, whose `IsOverWholeSpace` witness is `V.property`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 072W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/072W)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Abelian CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

variable (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})

/-- **The conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 07JJ], asked only at the thickenings of the whole of `X`.**
For every object `(U, T, δ)` of `Cris(X/S)` with `U ⟶ X` an isomorphism, and every `p > 0`, the
cohomology `H^p(Cris(X/S)/(U, T, δ), F)` of the localized site vanishes.

This is what step 4 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 07JK] evaluates `Vanishing07JJ` at; the ambient
scheme of such an object is automatically affine when `X` is, by
`SmallSite.isAffineObject_of_isOverWholeSpace`. -/
def Vanishing07JJWhole (F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) : Prop :=
  ∀ (A : CrystallineThickening S), IsOverWholeSpace S A →
    ∀ p : ℕ, 0 < p → IsZero ((overCohomologyFunctor S A p).obj ((restrictToOver S A).obj F))

variable [IsAffine S.X]

/-- The narrower hypothesis follows from `Vanishing07JJ`: a thickening of the whole of an affine
`X` has affine ambient scheme. -/
theorem vanishing07JJWhole_of_vanishing07JJ
    {F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}} (hF : Vanishing07JJ S F) :
    Vanishing07JJWhole S F :=
  fun A hA p hp => hF A (isAffineObject_of_isOverWholeSpace A hA).2 p hp

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 07JJ] at a thickening of the whole of `X`, read as the vanishing of right
derived sections.**  The proof is that of `isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJ`, with the
hypothesis evaluated at `wholeι V` rather than at an arbitrary affine object. -/
theorem isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJWhole
    {F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}} (hF : Vanishing07JJWhole S F)
    (V : WholeSpaceThickening S) (p : ℕ) (hp : 0 < p) :
    IsZero ((((sheafSections (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}).obj
      (op (wholeToAffineSubsite.obj V))).rightDerived p).obj ((restrictToAffine S).obj F)) :=
  have : IsAffine ((affineι S).obj (wholeToAffineSubsite.obj V)).obj.thickening.target.scheme :=
    (wholeToAffineSubsite.obj V).property.2
  ((hF ((affineι S).obj (wholeToAffineSubsite.obj V)) V.property p hp).of_iso
      (overCohomologyIsoRightDerivedSections S
        ((affineι S).obj (wholeToAffineSubsite.obj V)) F p).symm).of_iso
    (rightDerivedSectionsAffineIso S (wholeToAffineSubsite.obj V) F p).symm

/-- **The higher direct images onto the chaotic subsite vanish from the narrower hypothesis**:
`R^p f_* F|_{AffineCris} = 0` for `p > 0` whenever `F` satisfies `Vanishing07JJWhole`.

This is `isZero_higherDirectImageToWhole_of_vanishing07JJ` with the hypothesis cut down to the
objects the reduction evaluates it at, and it is therefore what step 4 of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 07JK] genuinely needs from [Stacks, Tag 07JJ]. -/
theorem isZero_higherDirectImageToWhole_of_vanishing07JJWhole
    {F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}} (hF : Vanishing07JJWhole S F)
    (p : ℕ) (hp : 0 < p) :
    IsZero ((higherDirectImageToWhole S p).obj ((restrictToAffine S).obj F)) :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.ChaoticSite.isZero_higherDirectImage_of_isZero_rightDerivedSections
    (affineTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} (wholeToAffineSubsite (S := S))
    ((restrictToAffine S).obj F) p
    fun V => isZero_rightDerivedSections_of_vanishing07JJWhole S hF V p hp

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

end

end
